                "subsection": "",
                "heading": "",
                "page_start": 1,
                "page_end": 1
            },
            "text": "This document outlines a reinforcement learning (RL) approach to optimize fraud detection in transaction systems. The goal is to improve precision, recall, and Gross Merchandise Value (GMV) impact compared to baseline models by refining reward functions and iteratively adjusting detection workflows.",
            "embedding": null,
            "embedding_text": null
        },
        {
            "metadata": {
                "chunk_uuid": "b4239479-c3a4-4597-8cb1-40de9404061a",
                "document_uuid": "4c459cae-9efa-4519-9b01-5a612cb9ace3",
                "chunk_index": 1,
                "authority": "Merchant_Fraud",
                "document_title": "2509.18719v1",
                "chapter": "",
                "chapter_title": "",
                "section": "",
                "subsection": "",
                "heading": "",
                "page_start": 1,
                "page_end": 1
            },
            "text": "The system uses RL agents to identify and block high-risk transactions, balancing the trade-off between blocking fraudulent activity (True Positives) and minimizing false positives (blocking legitimate transactions) and false negatives (missing fraud).",
            "embedding": null,
            "embedding_text": null
        },
